<!--
  sce:std/merge/lww_cell.scxml — one cell of a grid of last-writer-wins
  registers, as a replica holds it and as a write to it travels: where it is
  (`row`, `col`), what it holds, and the stamp of the write that put it
  there. The record type lww_write takes and returns (SCE_FORGE.md §4.12).

  `row` and `col` are the ids a grid gave its rows and columns, not their
  places: a place is decided by the order the rows and columns stand in
  (rga_insert), and an id does not move when another is inserted before it.
  They are as wide as an rga_node id, so an id rga_insert was given names a
  row or a column without narrowing.

  The stamp's three fields are hlc_timestamp's, spelled out rather than held
  as one: a record's fields are fixed-width scalars, so a record does not hold
  a record. A cell is stamped with the same widths a clock is, so a stamp read
  off a cell is a stamp hlc_compare orders.

  What a cell holds is a number or a formula, and it is one register either
  way: the write that wins the cell wins all of it, so a formula is data that
  merges as a number does, and what a formula means is not decided here. `op`
  says which it is.
  - 0 is a number, held in `value`; every field after the stamp is 0 or false.
  - Any other `op` is a formula over the operands a and b. An operand is a
    literal (`aRef` false, the number `aVal`) or a reference to the cell at
    (`aRow`, `aCol`) (`aRef` true); b is the same with `bRef`, `bRow`, `bCol`
    and `bVal`. The operations are 1, the value of operand a; 2, 3, 4 and 5,
    a + b, a - b, a * b and a / b; and 6, the sum of the cells inside the
    rectangle whose corners are the cells a and b name, which takes no literal.
  sheet_settle and sheet_show give a formula its value from the cells of the
  grid. An `op` they do not know is a fault they report rather than a failure,
  so a replica running a later version of the library cannot make an earlier
  one stop.
-->
<scxml xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/07/scxml"
       xmlns:sce="http://sce.dev/ext"
       version="1.0"
       sce:kind="event-schema"
       name="lww_cell"
       sce:event-name="merge.lww_cell">
  <datamodel>
    <data id="row" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="col" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="value" sce:type="int64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="wallTime" sce:type="int64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="counter" sce:type="uint32" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="nodeId" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="op" sce:type="uint8" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="aRef" sce:type="bool" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="aRow" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="aCol" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="aVal" sce:type="int64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="bRef" sce:type="bool" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="bRow" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="bCol" sce:type="uint64" sce:direction="in"/>
    <data id="bVal" sce:type="int64" sce:direction="in"/>
  </datamodel>
</scxml>
